# ============================================================================
# orca-serve-instance.env.template — PER-INSTANCE configuration (one per instance)
#
# Deployed to @PREFIX@/etc/instances/<instance>.env and loaded by
# orca-serve@<instance>.service as the SECOND EnvironmentFile= line — it overrides
# any overlapping key from the host orca-serve.conf. Copy to the instance name
# (e.g. default.env).
#
# Authoring rule: a value goes HERE if it differs by INSTANCE or VERSION.
# Host-wide values belong in orca-serve.conf; never duplicate a value in both.
#
# .template semantics: install-logging-setup.sh installs this file and creates the
# LIVE <instance>.env alongside it ONLY IF <instance>.env is absent — it must never
# clobber an operator-edited live env. The live file is what the unit's second
# EnvironmentFile= reads.
# ============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build / version identity
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The version the launch command exports for this instance. Upstream uses
# ORCA_VERSION as a version-skew identity (orcad remote launch hashes it), not as a
# build-selection pin. Set it to the build you deployed so client-vs-serve skew is
# diagnosable; the serve itself runs whatever binary ExecStart= points at.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ORCA_VERSION=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-instance listener pin
#
# The instance's port is NOT an env var: it is the `--port` flag in the unit's
# ExecStart=, substituted at install time from the installer's `--port` argument
# (e.g. `--port 6768`). Give each instance on a host a unique port; a collision is
# Bucket 3 (Server Config) in the troubleshooting matrix.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
